// Declarative Tailscale Serve + Funnel config for the Hermes mini-app router.
// Source of truth. Edit this file, then run:
//   ~/mini-apps/router/apply-tailscale-serve.sh
// Never run ad-hoc `tailscale serve ...` or `tailscale funnel ...` commands.
// They pile up additively and stomp each other across restarts.
//
// Funnel ports allowed by Tailscale: 443, 8443, 10000.
// Anything else is automatically tailnet-only.
//
// SECURITY RULE (non-negotiable): a port that is funnel'd is fully public.
// Only password-gated or token-gated upstreams may live on a funnel'd port.
// The admin UI (default 127.0.0.1:<admin-ui-port>) is passwordless and must
// NEVER appear under AllowFunnel.
//
// The apply script enforces that rule instead of trusting this comment. Every
// handler declares how its upstream is protected with "Gate": "password",
// "token", or "none". A handler on a funnel'd site must declare "password" or
// "token". A missing Gate on a funnel'd handler is a hard failure, so
// forgetting to annotate fails closed rather than publishing an upstream
// nobody reasoned about. Tailnet-only handlers do not need a Gate.
//
// Gate is an author-declared assertion, not a probe. The script cannot reach
// out and test an upstream, so a wrong Gate value still lets a bad config
// through. What it buys is that publishing something passwordless now takes a
// deliberate written claim that it is gated, instead of silence.
//
// ${HOST} is substituted with the node's MagicDNS name at apply time.
{
  "TCP": {
    "443": { "HTTPS": true }
  },
  "Web": {
    // Public front door: Caddy serves all apps + /hooks/. Apps are
    // password-gated by the auth sidecar.
    "${HOST}:443": {
      "Handlers": {
        // Caddy enforces forward_auth per app against the auth sidecar.
        "/": { "Proxy": "http://127.0.0.1:8080", "Gate": "password" },
        // The gateway hooks server requires a bearer token on every request.
        // Caddy injects it, so the caller does not present one at the edge.
        "/hooks/": { "Proxy": "http://127.0.0.1:8080/hooks/", "Gate": "token" }
      }
    }
    // Optional tailnet-only door for a passwordless admin UI. A port WITHOUT a
    // matching AllowFunnel entry stays tailnet-only. Add a "443"-style TCP entry
    // for 8443 and a Web handler pointing at the loopback admin port, e.g.:
    //   "TCP": { "8443": { "HTTPS": true } }
    //   "${HOST}:8443": { "Handlers": { "/": { "Proxy": "http://127.0.0.1:<admin-port>", "Gate": "none" } } }
    // Never list a passwordless port under AllowFunnel. The apply script will
    // refuse to compile a funnel'd handler whose Gate is "none" or missing.
  },
  "AllowFunnel": {
    "${HOST}:443": true
  }
}
